// COMPONENT MANIFEST — the single source of truth for each scene component's
// authoring contract: which data fields it reads, their budgets, the aliases an
// LLM is likely to invent, and a tiny valid example.
//
// Grounded field-by-field in src/types.ts (verified, not guessed). From here we
// derive (a) the LLM prompt's schema block, (b) the deterministic normalizer's
// alias/coercion map, (c) a field validator that catches "lints-clean-renders-
// blank". This is Fable's recommendation §3.1 — start with the core types, then
// grow coverage to all 136.
//
// Field spec: {t, req?, max?, note?}. t ∈ number|string|anchor|asset|asset[]|
//   items|object. `req` = required. `max` = char budget. Structural remaps that
//   can't be expressed as a flat/dotted rename (arrays, nested objects) live in
//   scripts/lib/normalize-spec.mjs REWRITES, keyed by type.
//
// `data_root: true`  → the component reads fields directly off scene.data.
// `data_key: 'foo'`  → the component reads scene.data.foo (a nested object).

